# Flutter Test Standards

- Prefer deterministic tests: avoid real time/network randomness unless explicitly mocked.
- Verify user-visible outcomes and state transitions, not just implementation details.
- Keep fixtures minimal and readable; centralize shared setup in helpers when repeated.
- For bug fixes, add or update a regression test that fails before and passes after.
- Avoid flaky patterns (`pumpAndSettle` without bounds, brittle text matching, implicit async waits).
- Name tests by behavior (`given_when_then` or equivalent clear phrasing).
- Keep test scope focused; use widget tests for UI behavior and unit tests for domain/service logic.

## Quick Example

```dart
// GOOD: bounded settling to reduce hangs/flakes
await tester.pump(const Duration(milliseconds: 100));
await tester.pumpAndSettle(const Duration(seconds: 2));
```
